\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces One circuit under each dependence rule. (a)~The circuit. (b)~For criteria $q_0$ and $q_2$, the dependences of the criterion (black) and the operations each rule keeps; $F$ is the criterion's fidelity at $\lvert 000\rangle $. QSlice's slice of $q_2$ has $F=1$ at $\lvert 000\rangle $ but is unsound at all 20 random product inputs tested. (c)~The edges each rule builds, with the backward slice of $q_0$ shaded. Def-use lets $o_4$ write only its target, so the slice of $q_0$ skips the kickback through $o_4$. QPDG adds edges between operations on the same entanglement component, which pull in $o_0$.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
